  "target_status": "grounded_rule_comment",
  "target_text": "Waterfall from an edge source around walls: a single red(2) SOURCE sits on a grid edge; its edge fixes the flow direction (top->down, bottom->up, left->right, right->left). Water flows inward cell by cell; blocked by a cyan(8) wall it spreads SIDEWAYS along the perpendicular axis until it can fall again, and stops at grid edges. Every traversed empty cell becomes 2."
